### W14. HR: onboarding, leave, payroll, offboarding [NEW]

**14a. Staff onboarding to working login** (user creation)

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A["HR: create staff record, contract, documents"] --> B["HR: request user account"]
  B --> C["Admin: create user linked to staff, assign role and department"]
  C --> D["System: invite link by email or SMS"]
  D --> E["Staff: set password, accept policy"]
  E --> F["Account active, first login logged"]
```

**14b. Leave**
`draft → submitted → supervisor_approved → hr_approved` (or `rejected`, `cancelled`). Balance checked on submit; approved leave blocks roster and appointment schedules for doctors; return-to-work closes the record.

**14c. Payroll (monthly)**
`draft → verified (HR) → approved (ACC) → approved (MGR) → posted → paid`. Inputs: attendance, overtime, leave, loans, allowances, tax and pension. Payslips are published only after posting. Any change after approval needs the whole chain again.

**14d. Offboarding**
HR records exit date and reason → clearance checklist (asset return, store and cash clearance) → final pay → Admin deactivates user on exit date (automatic) → sessions end → history kept.

**Audit events:** `hr.staff.create`, `.contract.update`, `.leave.approve`, `.payroll.approve`, `.payslip.view`, `admin.user.create`, `.user.deactivate`.

