### W15. User, role and access management [V1+]

| Request | Flow |
|---|---|
| New user | HR record → Admin creates user (W14a) |
| Change role | Supervisor request → Admin changes role → system records old and new set → notifies the user and the Auditor's dashboard |
| Temporary access | Admin adds role with end date; access expires automatically |
| Forgotten password | User requests reset link; or Admin resets and forces change at next login |
| Lockout | 5 failed attempts lock the account for 15 minutes; Admin may unlock |
| Deactivate | Admin sets inactive; user cannot sign in, history stays |
| Break-glass | Clinician opens a patient with no visit, enters reason, system logs and flags for review within 24 hours |

**Rules:** the system keeps at least one active admin; admins cannot change their own role or status [V1]; permission overrides for a single user are rare, time-limited and listed in the weekly access report.

---

### W16. Audit review [NEW]

**Daily:** AUD or MGR opens the exception report: voids and refunds, discounts above limit, payment-gate bypasses, break-glass access, stock write-offs, reopened visits, results amended, after-hours logins.
**Weekly:** access report (role changes, new accounts, inactive accounts); chain integrity check result.
**On demand:** "trace a patient" (every action on one patient), "trace a user" (every action by one user), "trace a document" (receipt, GRN, invoice history).
**Rules:** reviewing the audit log is itself logged; findings are recorded with owner and due date.

