## Part G. Exception playbook

| Situation | What to do in the system | Who |
|---|---|---|
| Patient registered twice | Request merge with both MRNs and reason | REC → ADM |
| Wrong patient chosen on an order | Cancel order with reason, re-order on right patient; if paid, refund request | DOC, CSH |
| Payment on wrong bill | Reversal with approval, re-take payment | CSH, ACC |
| Cash shortage at shift close | Record variance with reason; ACC reviews; repeated cases escalate to MGR | CSH, ACC |
| Result entered on wrong patient | Amend with reason; notify doctor; incident report | LAB |
| Expired drug found on shelf | Block batch, write-off with approval, review FEFO use | PHA, STO |
| Dispensed wrong drug | Reverse and correct dispense; incident; doctor and patient informed | PHA |
| Stock count variance | Recount; approve adjustment with reason; investigate | STO, ACC |
| System or internet down | Use paper forms; enter within one working day with paper reference; cashier uses numbered receipt book | All |
| Staff forgot password / locked out | Self-service reset, or Admin reset | ADM |
| Staff leaves suddenly | HR enters exit date today; Admin deactivates immediately | HRO, ADM |
| Suspected misuse of records | AUD runs user and patient trace; MGR decides action | AUD, MGR |
| Patient cannot pay for emergency care | Treat first, flag bypass, process credit or waiver afterwards | CSH, MGR |

